 362: -- IDENTICAL TO THE PREVIOUS MIGRATION'S, AND RE-STATED BECAUSE THE DROP TOOK THE OLD ONE WITH IT.
 363: --
 364: -- PostgreSQL grants EXECUTE on a new function to PUBLIC by default and every Data API role inherits
 365: -- that, so the freshly created function above is executable by `anon` until this revoke runs. The
 366: -- first migration found that by measuring with `has_function_privilege` rather than by reasoning,
 367: -- and the same measurement is repeated against this signature in the migration-replay capture.
 368: revoke execute on function public.complete_signup(uuid, text, text, text, inet, text, text[], integer, text, text, text, text) from public;
 369: grant execute on function public.complete_signup(uuid, text, text, text, inet, text, text[], integer, text, text, text, text) to service_role;
 370: 
 371: -- PostgREST caches the schema. Without this, the first call to the recreated function is a 404 from
 372: -- the schema cache rather than a real answer — and after a DROP the stale entry would name a
 373: -- signature that no longer exists. The added COLUMNS need the reload too: the cache describes
 374: -- `public.acknowledgments` as it was before this file ran.
